Bugfix: Previews no longer fail when a file has version previews

The preview cache of a file also holds the previews of its versions, in a
subfolder named after the version. Looking for a larger cached preview treated
that subfolder like a preview file, took its name apart as "width-height" and
divided by zero: the preview request ended with HTTP 500, and the log showed
"Undefined array key 1" and a DivisionByZeroError. Entries whose names carry no
dimensions are skipped now.

Broken image data, for example text in a .png file, no longer writes
"getimagesizefromstring(): Error reading from ..." to the log on every preview
attempt. The file is still rejected as before.
